# Line endings for the two launcher scripts, which are the only files here whose behaviour
# depends on them.
#
# A shell script with CRLF endings fails on macOS before it runs a line of its own: the kernel
# reads the shebang as `/bin/bash\r`, which does not exist, and reports "bad interpreter" naming
# a path the reader never typed. A .cmd is the mirror image, because cmd.exe has never parsed a
# multi-line parenthesised block reliably without CRLF.
#
# Both are pinned rather than left to core.autocrlf, which is a setting on whoever happens to be
# cloning. Nothing else is listed: a blanket `text=auto` would renormalise every file in the tree
# and bury this in a formatting commit.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.command text eol=lf
